Z||000000||rogergarrison||04-07-2001||07:44 PM||||I know lots of you use photopoint especially since Geo Cities sucks. But starting in May, photopoint is charging $20.00 for service and limits amount of pics. Ill be going elsewhere. MSN.com has a pretty ez to use photo svc. its limited too, but its free. Ive been using it for our club site to post and save pics. Think the limit is around a thousand pics, depending on their size.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||docprego||04-07-2001||08:18 PM||||Funny, I came here to post a similar topic.<P>When I got Photopoint's e-mail about the service not being free any longer, I got very aggravated.<BR> <BR>I understand companies don't exist for the benefit of humanity, they are around to make a buck.  But, this Internet business model where sites give you their service and say they are free and always will be, and then turn around and decide well, we're not free after all-that is starting to burn me a little.<P>First for me it was PayPal, then Auctionwatch, now Photopoint.  That is all of the services I signed up with under the pretense that they are "free" and always will be.<P>If you want to charge for your service, do it.  Don't tell me it's free, get me so used to using it that I feel trapped into paying for it after it is no longer "free"<P>Just my $.02<BR><P>------------------<BR>docprego<BR> <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_2.jpg">   <BR>White 1988 GT<BR>Sunroof, Power lumbar seat, Factory sub||||reg||1
